### Description
This Terraform program configures a Route 53 hosted zone and associates it with a VPC. The program includes the necessary resources and dependencies as inferred from the prompt. It creates a VPC with specific settings and a Route 53 zone, then associates the zone with the VPC.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "primary_vpc" {
  cidr_block           = "10.6.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
  enable_dns_support   = true
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "example_zone" {
  name = "example.com"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone_association" "zone_association" {
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.primary_vpc.id
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example_zone.zone_id
}
```

This configuration sets up a VPC with the specified CIDR block and DNS support, creates a Route 53 hosted zone for "example.com", and associates the zone with the VPC. The `aws_route53_zone_association` resource ensures that the DNS settings of the VPC are linked to the Route 53 zone.

