This Terraform program creates a DynamoDB table named `example_table` with a hash key `UserId` and a range key `GameTitle`. It also sets up DynamoDB Contributor Insights for this table. The table uses provisioned billing mode with read and write capacities set to 20.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  name           = "example_table"
  billing_mode   = "PROVISIONED"
  read_capacity  = 20
  write_capacity = 20

  hash_key = "UserId"
  range_key = "GameTitle"

  attribute {
    name = "UserId"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "GameTitle"
    type = "S"
  }
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights" "example_contributor_insights" {
  table_name = aws_dynamodb_table.example_table.name
}
```

This configuration sets up a DynamoDB table with the specified attributes and billing mode, and then enables Contributor Insights for that table. The `aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights` resource depends on the `aws_dynamodb_table` resource, ensuring that the table exists before enabling insights.

