### Description of the Terraform Program

The Terraform program defines the infrastructure necessary to create an Amazon SageMaker Space within a specific VPC and subnet. It includes the creation of a VPC, a subnet, an IAM role for execution, a SageMaker domain, and finally, the SageMaker space itself. The configuration ensures that all required attributes are set according to the AWS provider schema and addresses the error related to the `domain_name` in the SageMaker domain resource.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "sagemaker_vpc" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

resource "aws_subnet" "sagemaker_subnet" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.sagemaker_vpc.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_execution_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-execution-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_domain" "sagemaker_domain" {
  domain_name              = "example-domain"  # Changed to comply with valid characters
  auth_mode                = "IAM"
  subnet_ids               = [aws_subnet.sagemaker_subnet.id]
  vpc_id                   = aws_vpc.sagemaker_vpc.id

  default_user_settings {
    execution_role = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_execution_role.arn
  }
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_space" "sagemaker_space" {
  domain_id     = aws_sagemaker_domain.sagemaker_domain.id
  space_name    = "example_space"
  space_display_name = "Example Space"

  ownership_settings {
    owner_user_profile_name = "default"
  }

  space_settings {
    app_type = "JupyterServer"
  }

  space_sharing_settings {
    sharing_type = "Organization"
  }
}
```

### Explanation of Changes

1. **Domain Name Correction**: The `domain_name` in the `aws_sagemaker_domain` resource was changed from `"example_domain"` to `"example-domain"` to comply with the valid character requirements specified by AWS. Valid characters for `domain_name` are `a-z`, `A-Z`, `0-9`, and `-` (hyphen).

All other resources and configurations remain unchanged, ensuring that the Terraform program is deployable with Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`.

