### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster with the following specifications:
- Node type: `dax.r4.large`
- Replication factor: `1`
- IAM role for DAX to assume
- A parameter group named `my-dax-param-group`

The program includes the necessary IAM role and parameter group configurations to support the DAX cluster.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# Create an IAM role for DAX
resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_role" {
  name = "dax-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create a DAX parameter group
resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "dax_param_group" {
  name = "my-dax-param-group"

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_read_throughput_percentage"
    value = "50"
  }
}

# Create a DAX cluster
resource "aws_dax_cluster" "dax_cluster" {
  cluster_name       = "my-dax-cluster"
  iam_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.dax_role.arn
  node_type          = "dax.r4.large"
  replication_factor = 1
  parameter_group_name = aws_dax_parameter_group.dax_param_group.name
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up the necessary AWS resources to create a DAX cluster with the specified parameters. The IAM role allows DAX to perform its operations, and the parameter group provides configuration settings for the cluster.

