### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an HTTP listener that uses OIDC (OpenID Connect) authentication. The listener is configured to redirect unauthenticated requests to an OIDC provider for authentication. The necessary attributes for OIDC authentication, such as the authorization endpoint, client ID, client secret, issuer, token endpoint, and user info endpoint, need to be provided.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "front_end" {
  name               = "example-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"

  subnet_mapping {
    subnet_id = "subnet-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with your subnet ID
  }

  security_groups = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]  # Replace with your security group ID
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "front_end" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.front_end.arn
  port              = 80
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "authenticate-oidc"

    authenticate_oidc {
      authorization_endpoint = "https://example.com/auth"  # Replace with your OIDC provider's authorization endpoint
      client_id              = "your-client-id"            # Replace with your OIDC provider's client ID
      client_secret          = "your-client-secret"        # Replace with your OIDC provider's client secret
      issuer                 = "https://example.com"       # Replace with your OIDC provider's issuer
      token_endpoint         = "https://example.com/token"  # Replace with your OIDC provider's token endpoint
      user_info_endpoint     = "https://example.com/userinfo"  # Replace with your OIDC provider's user info endpoint
    }
  }
}
```

### Notes
- Replace the placeholder values for `subnet_id`, `security_groups`, `authorization_endpoint`, `client_id`, `client_secret`, `issuer`, `token_endpoint`, and `user_info_endpoint` with your actual values.
- Ensure that the security group associated with the ALB allows inbound traffic on port 80.
- This configuration assumes that you have already set up the necessary IAM roles and permissions for the ALB to interact with the OIDC provider.

